=== S: PAPER49's action, symbolically (sympy) ===
S1 FAIL K W_rem' = u^2/(a0-u): True; series(W used) = u**2*(a0**2/2 + a0*u/3 + u**2/4)/(K*a0**2) :: series == u^3/(3 a0 K) + u^4/(4 a0^2 K) (no u^2 term)  (W_rem starts at cubic order: no linear tether force about P = 0)
S2 FAIL Poisson True; P-eq False; rest g_N = g**2/(a0 + g) :: lap Phi = K(rho_b + div P); (grad Phi - K P) - R(u) + gamma lap P = 0; g_N = g^2/(g + a0)  (field equations and the n = 1 rest state)
S3 FAIL 1D d(force)/dP at P->0 = -K; 3D longitudinal (grad Phi - K P)_L = -I*K*rho_k/k, d/dP_L = 0 :: both == 0  (the tethered medium feels no self-gravity and no linear tether force (D-T on PAPER49's own action))
S4 PASS K|P| + R = a0 p/(1-p): True; stiffness coefficient Lstar**2/2; lap p = grad div p (curl-free): True :: identical to D10: grad Phi + (Lambda^2/2) grad div p = p/(1-|p|), Lambda = L*  (Z2's V3S and P4's T1 rows are this action's rest state)
S5 PASS completion kinetic eigenvalues [rho_b0, rho_c0]; BLT [[1,1],[1,0]] det -1 eig [-0.618034, 1.618034] :: completion positive definite; BLT det -1 (Z1 K1)  (PAPER49 + forced kinetic term has no ghost; BLT has one)
   medium gradient sector: omega^2 = gamma*k**2*rho_c0 >= 0 (gradient-stable); c_s^2 = gamma rho_c = 2 pi G rho_c L*^2
S6 FAIL growing exponent p = 1.0000 (largest eigenvalue 1.0000) :: 0.610 +- 0.005 (CFG938)  (delta ~ a^p in EdS with the medium feeling only the baryons)

